  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル教材。人物、出来事は架空の例であり、実在の調査や実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A school music club planned a small concert.",
          "ja": "学校の音楽部は小さなコンサートを計画した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The members practiced in their usual classroom.",
          "ja": "部員は普段の教室で練習した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They were happy with the sound of their song.",
          "ja": "歌の音に満足していた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Then they moved to a large hall for their final practice.",
          "ja": "その後最終練習のため大きなホールに移った。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Their teacher listened from the back of the room.",
          "ja": "教師は部屋の後方から聞いた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She could hear the piano clearly.",
          "ja": "ピアノははっきり聞こえた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "However, some of the singers' words were difficult to hear.",
          "ja": "しかし歌い手の言葉の一部は聞き取りにくかった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The students were surprised by her report.",
          "ja": "生徒はその報告に驚いた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "They asked a few friends to sit in different seats.",
          "ja": "数人の友人に違う席に座るよう頼んだ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The friends described what they could hear.",
          "ja": "友人は聞こえたものを説明した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The club changed the positions of the singers and the piano.",
          "ja": "部は歌い手とピアノの位置を変えた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They practiced again and listened to more feedback.",
          "ja": "再び練習し追加の意見を聞いた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "On the day of the concert, the members felt nervous.",
          "ja": "当日、部員は緊張した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They remembered the people sitting far from the stage.",
          "ja": "舞台から遠くに座る人々を思い出した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They tried to make the words clear without shouting.",
          "ja": "叫ばず言葉を明確にしようとした。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Afterward, the audience thanked them for the performance.",
          "ja": "その後観客は演奏に感謝した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The students learned something about music that day.",
          "ja": "その日生徒は音楽について何かを学んだ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A performance is not only about the people on stage.",
          "ja": "演奏は舞台上の人々だけに関するものではない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It is also about the people who listen.",
          "ja": "聞く人々に関するものでもある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The club decided to keep asking for feedback.",
          "ja": "部は意見を求め続けると決めた。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
